# ScrollAnchor — which end of a ScrollRoot's content the window holds
# (`ScrollRoot.anchor`, ui/Components; applied by ui/scrollRootSystem).
#
# - `start` (the default): content shorter than the window sits at its start
#   (the top), and a list opens at its first row.
# - `end`: the bottom-up list of a one-thumb UI or a chat. Content shorter
#   than the window sits at the window's end (the bottom, next to the controls
#   below it); a longer one opens scrolled to its end, and while the end is in
#   view a row added there keeps it in view. Scrolling away (a drag, the
#   wheel) lets go of the end; coming to rest at the end holds it again.
#   Rubber-banding and flings are the same as at the start.
#
#     "Tasks": { "ListView": { ... }, "ScrollRoot": { "axis": "y", "anchor": "end" } }
enum ScrollAnchor { start, end }
